        "content": "Accounting for nearly 24% of all daily foreign exchange turnover, EUR/USD is the undisputed heavyweight pair of global finance. Because both the United States and the Eurozone are multi-trillion-dollar diversified economies, EUR/USD does not trade on single commodity prices. Instead, its multi-month directional trend is governed by the **Transatlantic Sovereign Yield Spread**:\n\nYield Spread = Yield_US10Y - Yield_Bund10Y\n\nWhere:\n- Yield_US10Y represents the yield on 10-Year US Treasury benchmark bonds.\n- Yield_Bund10Y represents the yield on 10-Year German government bonds (Bunds), which serve as the risk-free benchmark for the European continent.\n\nWhen economic data causes US Treasury yields to rise faster than German Bund yields, capital moves across the Atlantic into dollar-denominated assets, driving EUR/USD downward. Conversely, when European yields outpace US yields, EUR/USD rallies.\n\nUnder the Fisher Equation, nominal yields reflect expected inflation plus the real interest rate:\n\ni = r + pi\n\nWhere i is nominal interest rate, r is real interest rate, and pi is expected inflation.\n\nIn 2027, institutional currency desks monitor four primary economic indicators to forecast EUR/USD momentum:\n1. **Federal Reserve vs. ECB Policy Rate Decisions**: The differential between the Fed Funds target rate and the ECB Deposit Facility rate establishes the baseline carry cost.\n2. **US Consumer Price Index (CPI) vs. Eurozone HICP**: The Harmonized Index of Consumer Prices (HICP) measures Eurozone inflation. If Eurozone core inflation decelerates while US inflation remains sticky, institutional desks price in ECB rate cuts ahead of the Fed, creating strong downward pressure on EUR/USD.\n3. **German ZEW & Ifo Business Climate Surveys**: As Europe's industrial engine, Germany's forward-looking business sentiment indices provide leading indicators for European GDP growth.\n4. **US Non-Farm Payrolls (NFP)**: Strong US job growth signals domestic economic resilience, validating higher-for-longer Federal Reserve policy.\n\nCalculate exact lot sizes tailored to EUR/USD and cross pair pip values with our [forex position size calculator and risk management guide](/blog/forex-position-size-calculator-risk-management-guide)."
